  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enterprise Development and Growth Enhanced (EDGE)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Zambia):  The Enterprise Development and Growth Enhanced (EDGE) activity provides technical assistance to financial intermediaries to strengthen their capacity to lend to rural enterprises and improve management capacities of small and medium sized agricultural enterprises (SMEs). FY 2022 funds will support activities working with finance institutions to design financial products and services relevant to the needs of rural enterprises; strengthen their lending capacity; and design ways to simplify the lending process to reduce the costs of lending. It will also address challenges that private sector enterprises face in opening up opportunities to increase their own customer base and ultimately increase their demand for and effective utilization of financial services.  Activities include strengthening the ability of banks and finance institutions to serve SMEs and catalyze the growth of non-bank financial institutions and making SMEs and their products more competitive. The activity also works to strengthen SME management and marketing capacity and improve network input/output relationships. Through a business advisor network, the activity works to support agricultural SMEs to reduce costs and increase efficiency by strengthening managerial capacity and improving their ability to seek and qualify for finance. More efficient and competitive SMEs will increase employment in general, and for youth and women. This approach will increase the profitability of agricultural SMEs by facilitating greater revenue through increased sales and expanding access to new markets with premium sales prices. EDGE supports the Global Food Security Strategy objectives of Reducing Rural Poverty through increased agriculture-led economic growth and expanded markets and trade and the USAID/Zambia Country Development Cooperation Strategy Development Objective 2: Rural Poverty Reduced Through Enterprise-Driven Inclusive Economic Growth.</narrative>
  </description>
